      "jobId": "88781f5f-812f-4b69-b54a-2280a7abee77",
      "prompt": "A single regular hexagonal deep ocean tile for a diorama with exactly six straight flat edges, 32 m across, on a plain neutral grey studio backdrop. Open temperate sea with layered gentle waves, a few white foam flecks on crests, clear water tinted pale turquoise in the shallows and deep teal-blue where deep, sun glints, soft caustics on the shallow bed. On every side the hexagon side wall shows the water column in cross-section like clear tinted resin, turquoise at the top fading to deep blue at the bottom, never an empty gap. Through the clear side walls a pale sandy shelf rises toward one edge and slopes down to a darker sandy seabed with scattered pebbles. Photoreal PBR rendering with plain sand and pebbles only, stylized-real diorama miniature, real PBR materials, slightly exaggerated proportions, soft noon sun, neutral grey studio background, 35 degree three-quarter view"
    },
